# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

> **Business Edition only.** This endpoint does not exist in Portainer CE.

Inspects one Omni machine, including the hardware and network detail needed to write a `portainer_omni_cluster` machine block.

## Example Usage

```hcl
data "portainer_omni_machine" "cp_1" {
  credential_id = portainer_cloud_credentials.omni.id
  machine_name  = "cp-1"
}

output "system_disk" {
  value = one([for d in data.portainer_omni_machine.cp_1.block_devices : d.linux_name if d.system_disk])
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Notes on Arguments and Attributes

- `block_devices`: Block devices Omni sees, with `linux_name`, `model`, `size`, `type` and `system_disk`.
- `memory_modules`: Memory modules, with `description` and `size_mb`.
- `processors`: Processors, with `description`, `manufacturer`, `core_count`, `thread_count` and `frequency`.
- `network_links`: Network links, with `linux_name`, `hardware_address`, `link_up` and `speed_mbps`.
